# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the MPI runs.
#
# Open MPI keeps its runtime state allocated until the process exits, so every
# rank reports a few KiB from MPI_Init, the PMIx client and the libevent
# progress thread it spawns, none of it ours. Matching by library keeps the
# suppressions stable across Open MPI builds, and a leak in our own code never
# has these on its stack. The Dockerfile builds Open MPI with its components
# internal, so none of this is behind a dlclosed module the symbolizer would
# render as "<unknown module>", which no template here could ever match.
leak:libmpi.so
leak:libopen-pal.so
leak:libopen-rte.so
leak:libpmix.so
# Bundled into the libraries above, so their frames name the source file.
leak:hwloc
leak:libevent
